<title>UK: Copper steadier in LME rings, cash sought.</title>
<headline>Copper steadier in LME rings, cash sought.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Testing the $2,415 resistance and continuing recovery from seven-week low on Wednesday. Some cash buying seen, spreads tight. Cash/threes $130 backw.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Advance stalls at $1,580. NICKEL - Cuts losses.</p>
<p>ZINC - Firm above $1,400, briefly at new seven-year high.</p>
<p>TIN - Drifts back, still steadier. LEAD/ALLOY  - Quiet.</p>
</text>
